<title>USA: Grand Premier Financial Inc Q3 net off.</title>
<headline>Grand Premier Financial Inc Q3 net off.</headline>
<dateline>WAUCONDA, Ill. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			 $ 0.09		    $0.22</p>
<p> Net			  2,113		    4,712</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  20,151		   20,035</p>
<p>			9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 $ 0.43		   $ 0.56</p>
<p> Net			  9,494		   12,032</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  20,123		   20,112</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 earnings were reduced by $1.4 million for anticipated contract and lease terminations as well as anticipated severance benefits related to staff reductions and by an expense provision of $1.5 million for possible loan losses. During the quarter, the company also had $543,000 in investment banking and professional fees taken in connection with the August 22, 1996 merger of Northern Illinois Financial Corp and Premier Financial Services Inc into Grand Premier Financial Inc.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
